# Styling Conventions

## Tailwind CSS v4

- Utility-first approach with the new `@import "tailwindcss"` syntax.
- PostCSS plugin: `@tailwindcss/postcss`.
- CSS variables defined in `src/styles/index.css` using `oklch()` color space.

## Dark-Only Theme

The app forces dark mode (`document.documentElement.classList.add("dark")`). All color choices assume a dark background. Do not add light-mode variants.

## Color Palette

| Role | Colors |
|---|---|
| Background | slate-950 |
| Cards / surfaces | slate-900 |
| Borders | slate-800 |
| Primary actions | blue-500 / blue-600 |
| Success | green-500 |
| Error / destructive | red-500 |
| Warning | yellow-500 |
| Compose/project accent | purple-500 |
| Security accent | orange-500 |

## Class Merging

Always use the `cn()` helper from `src/components/ui/utils.ts` for conditional classes:

```typescript
import { cn } from "@/components/ui/utils";

<div className={cn("rounded-lg p-4", isActive && "border-blue-500")} />
```

## UI Primitives (shadcn/ui)

- Located in `src/components/ui/`.
- Built with CVA (`class-variance-authority`) for variant styling.
- Support `asChild` via Radix `Slot` for composition.
- No CSS modules, no styled-components — pure Tailwind utilities everywhere.
